  "worked_solution": "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{2x}+6\\cdot {e}^{2x} & =25x\\cdot {e}^{2x} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{2x}-25x\\cdot {e}^{2x}+6\\cdot {e}^{2x} & =0 \\\\ (4{x}^{2}-25x+6)\\cdot {e}^{2x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-25x+6=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{e}^{2x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $4{x}^{2}-25x+6=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(4x-1)(x-6)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=\\frac{1}{4},x=6.$\n\n- The equation ${e}^{2x}=0$ has no solutions because ${e}^{2x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{and}\\,x=6.\n$$",
